⍝ ZZ72_Regression.tc
⍝ ══════════════════

⍝@ test3.

      ⍝ Blake McBride's Bugs33 report (9 items): the ∇-editor (Nabla.cc).
      ⍝ #8 ([∆n1 n2 ...]) is a documented gap, see apl2lrm.tc #45/#46.
      ⍝
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS



      ⍝ #1 an existing function that is only displayed (∇F[⎕]∇) is not fixed
      ⍝ again, so its creation time stays the same
      ⍝
      ⊣⎕FX 'FOO' 'A←1' 'B←2'





      T1←2 ⎕AT 'FOO'





      ⊣⎕DL 1.1





      ∇FOO[⎕1]∇
    ∇
[0]   FOO
[1]   A←1





      T1≡2 ⎕AT 'FOO'
1





      )ERASE FOO T1







      ⍝ #2 [→] ends editing without establishing anything (LRM p. 392): ⎕STOP
      ⍝ and the creation time of an existing function stay, and a new
      ⍝ function is not created
      ⍝
      ∇FOO
      A←1
      B←2
      ∇





      2 ⎕STOP 'FOO'





      T1←2 ⎕AT 'FOO'





      ⊣⎕DL 1.1





      ∇FOO
      [1] X←99
      [→]





      ⎕STOP 'FOO'
2





      T1≡2 ⎕AT 'FOO'
1





      ⎕CR 'FOO'
FOO      
      A←1
      B←2





      ∇NEWFN
      A←1
      [→]





      ⎕NC 'NEWFN'
0





      )ERASE FOO T1







      ⍝ #3 [N] without text only positions the editor at line N (LRM p. 386)
      ⍝
      ∇FOO
      A←1
      B←2
      C←3
      ∇





      ∇FOO
      [2]
      ∇





      ∇FOO[2]
      X←9
      ∇





      ⎕CR 'FOO'
FOO      
      A←1
      X←9
      C←3





      )ERASE FOO







      ⍝ #4 a ∇ in a comment neither truncates the line nor closes the editor;
      ⍝ a line with a comment is never closed by ∇ (LRM p. 388)
      ⍝
      ∇FOO
      A←1
      B←2
      ∇





      ∇FOO
      [1] A←1 ⍝ needs ∇ here
      C←3 ⍝ comment∇
      ∇





      ⎕CR 'FOO'
FOO                 
A←1 ⍝ needs ∇ here  
      C←3 ⍝ comment∇





      )ERASE FOO







      ⍝ #5 a bad header line [0] gives DEFN ERROR when not interactive (as a
      ⍝ bad body line does); the function stays unchanged
      ⍝
      ∇FOO
      A←1
      ∇





      ∇FOO
      [0] 1BADHDR
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇FOO
         ^





      ⎕CR 'FOO'
FOO      
      A←1





      )ERASE FOO







      ⍝ #6 the line after [2147483647] is [2147483647.1] (no overflow)
      ⍝
      ∇FOO
      [2147483647] A←1
      B←2
      ∇





      ⎕CR 'FOO'
FOO      
A←1      
      B←2





      )ERASE FOO







      ⍝ #7 ∇F[⎕]⍫ displays, closes, and locks
      ⍝
      ∇LCK
      A←1
      B←2
      ∇





      ∇LCK[⎕1]⍫
    ∇
[0]   LCK
[1]         A←1





      3 ⎕AT 'LCK'
1 1 1 1





      )ERASE LCK







      ⍝ #8 (implemented 2026-10-08): the list forms [⎕n1 n2 ...] and [∆n1 n2
      ⍝ ...] and the open-ended ranges [⎕n-] and [∆n-] (LRM pp. 389-391).
      ⍝ Unlike the LRM, line numbers out of order (also repeated ones) are
      ⍝ rejected.
      ⍝
      ∇LST
      A←1
      B←2
      C←3
      D←4
      E←5
      ∇





      ∇LST[⎕2 4 9]∇
[2]         B←2
[4]         D←4





      ∇LST[∆0 1 4]∇





      ⎕CR 'LST'
LST      
      B←2
      C←3
      E←5





      ∇LST[∆3 1]∇
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇LST[∆3 1]∇
                ^





      ∇LST[∆2 2]∇
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇LST[∆2 2]∇
                ^





      ∇LST[⎕3-1]∇
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇LST[⎕3-1]∇
                ^





      ∇LST[∆2 7]∇
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇LST[∆2 7]∇
                ^





      ∇LST[2⎕3 4]∇
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇LST[2⎕3 4]∇
                 ^





      ∇LST[∆3-]∇





      ⎕CR 'LST'
LST      
      B←2
      C←3





      )ERASE LST







      ⍝ #9 a line number is a number: [1.0] is line [1], [2.10] is [2.1]
      ⍝
      ∇FOO
      F1←1
      F2←2
      [1.0] REPL←99
      [2.10] I←1
      ∇





      ⎕CR 'FOO'
FOO       
REPL←99   
      F2←2
I←1       





      )ERASE FOO





